More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (631–640)
631. Improper Validation of API Rate Limits per User
Per‑User Rate Limit Bypass
Applications enforce rate limits globally but not per user, allowing attackers to abuse APIs using multiple accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
632. Insecure Handling of Temporary Session Tokens
Temporary Session Token Exposure
Temporary session tokens remain valid longer than intended or can be reused.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
633. Improper Validation of Webhook Payloads
Webhook Payload Manipulation
Webhook payloads are not verified properly, allowing attackers to send forged requests.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
634. Insecure Handling of API Response Headers
Sensitive Header Information Disclosure
Response headers leak server details, internal IPs, or software versions.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
635. Improper Validation of Third-Party Integrations
Third‑Party Integration Authorization Bypass
External integrations access user data without proper permission validation.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
636. Insecure Handling of Internal API Documentation
Internal API Documentation Exposure
Private documentation endpoints reveal internal APIs and parameters.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
637. Improper Validation of Data Import APIs
Data Import Manipulation
Attackers manipulate imported data to affect backend processing or bypass validation.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
638. Insecure Handling of Password Reset Notifications
Password Reset Notification Leak
Password reset notifications expose sensitive links or tokens.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
639. Improper Validation of Subscription Upgrade APIs
Subscription Upgrade Manipulation
Attackers upgrade accounts to premium services without payment.
💰 Typical payout: $700 – $12,000
640. Insecure Handling of System Audit Logs
Audit Log Exposure
Audit logs expose sensitive system activity or administrative operations.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
